              "text": "When Acne Needs More Than Skincare\n\nAcne can sometimes improve with appropriate skincare, but persistent, recurrent or severe acne may require medical treatment.\n\nSeeking treatment early can help address three common problems:\n\nRecurring breakouts \u2013 treating the underlying acne can help reduce the cycle of new breakouts appearing week after week.\nSkincare trial and error \u2013 using multiple products without understanding your acne type may irritate the skin or make it difficult to identify what is actually helping.\nAcne marks and scars \u2013 prolonged inflammation, particularly from cystic or nodular acne, increases the risk of pigmentation and permanent indented scarring.\n\nOnce an indented acne scar has formed, restoring the damaged skin becomes considerably more difficult than treating the active acne that caused it and often requires multiple treatments over time.\n\nAcne treatment does not always have to be complicated. Depending on its severity, early management may begin with appropriate skincare and topical medications, while more severe acne may require a more comprehensive medical approach.\n\n\ud83c\udfa5 In this video, Dr Chiam explains why treating persistent or severe acne early can help reduce breakouts and minimise the risk of permanent scarring.\n\n#acne #acnetreatment #acnescars #cysticacne #teenageacne #skinhealth #doctorexplains #ensoulclinic\n\nTel: +00 0000 0000\nWhatsapp: +00 0000 0000\nEmail: contact@scrubbed.invalid\nFor more information, visit www.ensoulclinic.com",
